        <item>
            <title>1.0.9</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:15:42 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>121</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.9</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font: -apple-system-body, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }
  h3 { font-size: 13px; margin: 14px 0 6px; }
  h3:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  ul { margin: 6px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 5px; }
  p { margin: 6px 0; }
</style>
<ul>
<li>Clicking the menu bar icon no longer drags the MacBreeze window in front of whatever you were working in.</li>
<li>Each fan&#x27;s real speed now stays on screen while an app automation is running, instead of disappearing exactly when you want to check it.</li>
<li>Changing a rule between &quot;While Running&quot; and &quot;While Frontmost&quot; now takes effect immediately, rather than waiting for that app to quit.</li>
<li>New switch on the App Automations page: whether the app you are working in takes the fans from a rule higher in the list, or the list order decides everything.</li>
<li>An open fan curve stays open — when you visit another page, and when you quit and come back.</li>
<li>The dashboard window now keeps one size, and Preferences can open it centred on screen or put it away when you switch desktop.</li>
<li>This window now lists every version you missed, not only the newest one, and opens in the middle of the screen.</li>
<li>The dashboard dims behind this window, and the current-temperature dot on the fan curve is no longer hidden by its own dashed line.</li>
</ul>]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://macbreeze.app/downloads/MacBreeze-1.0.9.dmg" length="3340819" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="aKEtS+cF8UK7Y78GlZNjI2P7mJcCLo64rnwRY9sPffGFWSLz/Fv3+fRri9a2gDRG7Zjh+LTDZ3BFbK9MeFtWAQ=="/>
        </item>
